## Country & Fiscal Regimes (Multi-Country)

Austria (`company_settings.country = 'AT'`) remains the production fiscal path (RKSV/TSE/FinanzOnline). Hub: [`docs/COUNTRIES.md`](../../docs/COUNTRIES.md). Detail: [`docs/FISCAL_GERMANY.md`](../../docs/FISCAL_GERMANY.md), [`docs/FISCAL_SWITZERLAND.md`](../../docs/FISCAL_SWITZERLAND.md), [`docs/EINVOICING_EU.md`](../../docs/EINVOICING_EU.md). Cutover: [`docs/COUNTRY_LAYER_CUTOVER.md`](../../docs/COUNTRY_LAYER_CUTOVER.md). Paket 30-d (OSS destination rates) is done.

- **AT:** production fiscal path. Unchanged.
- **DE:** contract (`IKassenSicherheitService`) plus the Development soft signer (`SoftKassenSicherheitService`) plus fiskaly-de outbound HTTP (`FiskalyDeKassenSicherheitService`) plus `PaymentService` wiring via `IFiscalSignatureRouter` (`SignDeAsync` → `SignAsync`). Not production-ready: DSFinV-K (`ExportDsfinvkAsync` is a PUT only), DE offline (§13 of [`docs/FISCAL_ROUTER_PLAN.md`](../../docs/FISCAL_ROUTER_PLAN.md)), and DE BelegNr as a production fiscal number (`DeReceiptSequenceService.FormatDeBelegNr` allocates `de_receipt_sequences`; it is not the Austrian RKSV Beleg). Signatures go to `de_tse_signatures`; `payment_details.TseSignature` stays null for DE. Do not enable `Fiscal.KassenSicherheitDe` for a real tenant. `CountryFeatureFlagDefaults.TryGet` returns false for that flag, so a DE tenant stays off until an explicit tenant override.
- **CH:** MWST rates (`ICountryTaxTypeRegistry` / `ChMwstEffectiveRates`) plus QR-Rechnung payload (`QrRechnungBuilder`) plus PDF (`QrRechnungPdf`). `SwitzerlandTaxStrategy.ProjectFiscalTaxSets` uses `ChTaxSetMapper`. `SwitzerlandInvoiceStrategy.AllocateReceiptNumberAsync` uses `ch_receipt_sequences` (`CH-{slug}-{register}-{seq}`). Not production-ready: bank submit (`QrRechnung:BankSubmit:Enabled` defaults false; `true` fails Production/Staging startup) and the print gaps in `ChQrKnownGaps.json` (`ChQrKnownGapsTests`).
- **EU:** UBL builder (`En16931UblXmlBuilder`, `EU_DEFAULT` only) plus the embedded Schematron validator (`En16931Schematron`, `En16931InvoiceValidationService`). Not production-ready: XRechnung (`NotImplementedXrechnungXmlBuilder`), ZUGFeRD (`NotImplementedZugferdXmlBuilder`), and Peppol submission. `EInvoicing.Peppol` stays in `FeatureFlagNames.Reserved` and out of `All`. `Peppol:ReservedExit` can mark one canary. `SubmitAsync` opens HTTP only for that tenant when `Provider=storecove` and `Peppol:Storecove:Environment=TEST`. HTTP 2xx is `Sent`, not an ACK.

- Resolve country from `CompanySettings.Country` (column `country`, `NOT NULL DEFAULT 'AT'`, added in `20260723190000_AddTenantSettingsHistory`). Unknown/legacy value = AT. **Never add a `CountryCode` column or a second country field.** `VatRegime`, `BillingCountry`, and `TaxExempt` shipped in migration `20260916110000_AddCompanySettingsCountryBilling` — that file is the only later country-schema change on `company_settings`. Issue-time snapshots live on invoices/receipts/payment_details (`CountryCodeAtIssue` / `VatRegimeAtIssue`); do not rewrite historical rows on country change. `CountryLayerBypassGateTests` enforces this (CI job step in [`.github/workflows/backend-unit-tests.yml`](../../.github/workflows/backend-unit-tests.yml), on every PR that touches `backend/**`, including `backend/Models/Countries/**`, `backend/Services/Countries/**`, and `backend/Data/AppDbContext.cs`).
- `ICountryProfileRegistry` (seeds: AT, DE, CH, registry-only `EU_DEFAULT`) is **shipped and called** (strategy resolvers, `IFeatureFlagService` country defaults, `GET /api/admin/countries`, `IVatIdValidator`). `GetOrDefault` → AT for unknown/legacy codes; `Get` throws `UNKNOWN_COUNTRY_CODE`. Profiles hold no VAT rates. AT seed mirrors the live company-settings defaults and is pinned by tests.
- `ITaxStrategy` / `IInvoiceStrategy` are **wired** into `PaymentService` and `InvoiceService` (Paket 30-c). `TseService` tax-set projection and `RksvSpecialReceiptService` stay Austria-only (`NotSupportedException`). Offline BelegNr goes through `IInvoiceStrategy.AllocateReceiptNumberAsync` (Paket 30-b). AT + `EU_REVERSE_CHARGE` routes to EuDefault strategies (Paket 12-c). Unknown pairs throw `UNKNOWN_TAX_REGIME` (never an AT fallback). Do not fork `PaymentService` or `TseService` internals.
- The Austrian strategies are **adapters only**: `CalculateTax` → `CartMoneyHelper`, `ProjectFiscalTaxSets` → `RksvTaxSetMapper`, `AllocateReceiptNumberAsync` → `ISequenceReservationService`, `BuildInvoiceDocumentAsync` → `IReceiptService`, VAT-ID shape → `CountryProfile`. Never restate a rate, rounding rule, or bucket rule inside a strategy. TSE signing input / machine code / QR stay out of `IInvoiceStrategy`. DE/CH `CalculateTax` uses `ICountryTaxTypeRegistry`. `GermanyTaxStrategy.ProjectFiscalTaxSets` delegates to `DeTaxSetMapper`. `GermanyInvoiceStrategy.AllocateReceiptNumberAsync` uses `DeReceiptSequenceService`. `EuDefaultTaxStrategy.ProjectFiscalTaxSets` and `EuDefaultInvoiceStrategy.AllocateReceiptNumberAsync` still throw `NotImplementedException`.
- Gate country features with `IFeatureFlagService` (`tenant_settings` keys `FeatureFlags:{Name}`). Country-derived defaults: tenant override → profile. `Fiscal.RksvAt` is always on for AT and cannot be disabled (**locked**; name is in `FeatureFlagNames`).
- Tenant create requires an ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country in the request payload, persisted to `company_settings.country` (FA `CreateTenantWizard`: country step then form). Super Admin tenant detail: Country & Fiscal Regime card (`PATCH /api/admin/tenants/{id}/country`). Non-AT tenants must not enable RKSV/TSE.
- VAT-ID regexes, rates, and labels live in CountryProfile seeds / `ICountryTaxTypeRegistry` — not in controllers or FA form constants. `EU_DEFAULT` is registry-only, not selectable.
- POS vertical profiles are product configuration, separate from country regimes and `FeatureFlagNames`; schema, seeds, override merge rules, and APIs: [`docs/VERTICAL_PROFILES.md`](../../docs/VERTICAL_PROFILES.md).
- **One VAT-ID literal:** `Models/Countries/VatIdPatterns` (`Austria` = `^ATU\d{8}$`, …) is referenced by the CountryProfile seeds, the two `[RegularExpression]` attributes, and every runtime consumer (`PaymentService`, `TenantSettingsService`, fiskaly services, `InvoiceController`). Never declare a local `^ATU\d{8}$` or another country's VAT-ID regex again. `CountryLayerBypassGateTests` scans production sources and fails with the offending paths when a literal appears outside `VatIdPatterns` and `CountryProfileRegistry`. The same gate asserts every `ITaxStrategy` / `IInvoiceStrategy` resolves for AT, DE, CH, and `EU_DEFAULT`, and that an unknown pair throws `UNKNOWN_TAX_REGIME`. Matching is **strict** (no trim, no case folding); normalization stays at the call site that needs it.


## Related prohibitions
- Do not weaken validation, auditability, authorization, or fiscal guarantees.
- Do not hardcode country codes, VAT rates, or VAT-ID regexes outside `CountryProfile` seeds.
- Do not enable `Fiscal.KassenSicherheitDe` or `QrRechnung:BankSubmit` for a real tenant until the corresponding package is marked production-ready in `docs/COUNTRIES.md` §16.
- Cart → Payment → Receipt → DailyClosing, TSE/RKSV signing, voucher ledger, and FinanzOnline outbox SOAP are high-risk flows.
